    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:569e72e117968fcc",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "6f7e7daec7bceef027804e1a5fd1b58a841655d4f9d36c8e8b871461f56f0afa",
      "text": "Early wake up for ground transfer to the port above the falls. Navigate in motorized Indian canoes on the Carrao River where you will enjoy a walk in the savannah and visit the pool of joy. Next you enter the much smaller Churun river and head up to the Devil’s Canyon – a spectacular gorge with soaring vertical walls and numerous cascades flowing down its faces. Our route follows the river that receives the waters of Angel Falls. This is a place of incredible energy and beauty. Arrival to Ratoncito Island where you are rewarded with a close-up view of Angel Falls, whose waters free-fall from almost 1000 meters through the air before crashing into the rocks below! Then hike 1 hour through tropical vegetation filled with small orange and red rivers, huge trees with hanging orquids and bromeliads and rocks painted in green moss, until we reach Laime lookout point. After breathtaking views of the worlds tallest waterfall, lunch and back to Canaima, Waku lodge (B,L,D)",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "word_exact",
        "fileId": "1tHIW9z-qNCjM-DWY_dFZ5mjV1KtslBh9",
        "documentSha256": "29a97c9ab88c3704dacaec1af332ab623ca371e1b777ea21b79cdf1a53f6d6fa",
        "paragraphs": [
          {
